Package: SIMPLICA
Title: Simplivariate Component Analysis
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person("Jos", "Hageman", email = "jos.hageman@wur.nl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Identifies coherent biclusters in numeric data matrices using
    simplivariate component analysis. Components are extracted sequentially
    using a binary genetic algorithm to select subsets of rows and columns,
    followed by residual deflation. Six built-in component patterns are
    supported: constant, row, column, additive, multiplicative, and
    additive-multiplicative. Components may overlap, and missing values
    are handled without imputation. Cross-validation can be used for
    pattern selection after component extraction. User-defined component
    patterns and corresponding model complexity specifications can also
    be supplied. The method builds on simplivariate models as introduced
    in Hageman et al. (2008) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0003259> and is
    related to biclustering frameworks as reviewed by Madeira and Oliveira
    (2004) <doi:10.1109/TCBB.2004.2>.
